1. Overview
Project Name: SIEM Detection and Forensic Analysis of a Simulated Account Compromise
Project Description
The purpose of this project is to simulate an account compromise within a controlled virtual lab environment and investigate the incident using SIEM and digital forensic techniques. A series of suspicious activities will be performed on a test system, such as repeated failed login attempts, a successful unauthorized login, account changes, access to sensitive test files, file modification or deletion, and suspicious network activity.
Security logs and other evidence will be collected and analyzed using a SIEM platform and forensic tools. The team will reconstruct the timeline of the incident, determine which activities were detected, identify evidence supporting the investigation, and evaluate the effectiveness of the monitoring system. The project will focus mainly on security analysis, incident reconstruction, and reporting rather than performing an advanced cyberattack.
Objectives
Create a controlled virtual environment for the simulated incident.
Generate realistic suspicious security events.
Collect system and security logs using a SIEM platform.
Identify and analyze alerts generated by the SIEM.
Perform forensic analysis on relevant evidence.
Reconstruct the timeline of the simulated account compromise.
Compare the actual activities performed with what the SIEM and forensic investigation detected.
Identify gaps or weaknesses in detection.
Develop recommendations for improving security monitoring and incident response.
Produce a professional final incident analysis report.
Success Criteria
The project will be considered successful if the team can successfully generate and collect security events, identify evidence of suspicious activity, reconstruct the majority of the simulated incident, evaluate the SIEM's ability to detect the activity, and produce a final report clearly explaining the findings and recommendations.
